  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Line P (PERD Project) - Oceanic carbon dioxide, 1988-present",
  "description": "Observations of large-scale changes in oceanic PC02 and supporting data of oceanographic properties and carbonate chemistry. May also include other lines and other projects (Line Z, Line R, Line PE, JGOFS, WOCE, Seamounts, Alaskan Gyre, Eddy, ).\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Determination of the penetration of CO2 into the water column.\n\nSupplemental information: Risk Justification: Custodian will be leaving soon and has a large quantity of data not secured in a regional data centre. Risk of Loss: High Impact Justification: Long term time series (more than 10 years) Impact of Loss: High Recommended Action: Obtain access to data and bring to archives Additional Info: Freon data have been partly published; data will be made available after publication. PCO2 data (1973-1999) have been sent to the OSAP archive. Much of the productivity and chlorophyll data have been published, will be made available. DOC data are in press, and will be made available. DON data have been written up into a paper which has not yet been submitted for publication. TCO2 and Talkalinity profiles have been made available (1972-1997) and TCO2 and Talkalinity surface data (1972-1990) have been made available. C13 and O-18 data are custody of C.S. Wong. Storage Requirements: 50MB+unknown",
