  "measurementTechnique": "Logical consistency: Standardization of chemical instrumentation with known or commercially prepared standards.\n\nCompleteness: Dataset Complications: Some DOC data are questionable. Meteorological data from NOAA buoy at Station P no longer freely available. Portable met. station on ship gives apparent measures of wind speed and direction for PCO2, must be corrected for ship`s heading, speed, etc. PCO2 originally measured by IR spectrophotometer, then by gas chromatograph, now using a non-dispersive IR analyzer. C13 and O-18 data are custody of C.S. Wong. Electronic Data Complications: Temperature, salinity, oxygen and nutrient data on IOS archived database are not quite conforming to IOS Header format, and are therefore difficult to search. All of the magtapes are older than their guaranteed physical lifespan. The last attempt to retrieve data from a magtape was successful (July 7, 2000).\n\nProcessing step (Unknown): Unknown",
  "usageInfo": {
    "@type": "CreativeWork",
    "name": "Use and access constraints (from the FGDC record; no license is granted)",
    "text": "Use constraints: Temperature, salinity, dissolved oxygen, and nutrient data are stored on the OSAP database, Departmentally accessible. Other data will be available after publication/quality checked (see Additional Information, below) Access constraints: May Be Private Distribution liability: [unknown]"
  },
